Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:01.33,Caption,,0,0,0,,Moon gone. Gravity lingers.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.33,0:00:02.28,Caption,,0,0,0,,Lunar tides start changing
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.28,0:00:03.22,Caption,,0,0,0,,next.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.22,0:00:04.70,Caption,,0,0,0,,Known physics says the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.70,0:00:06.17,Caption,,0,0,0,,mechanism is orbital angular
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.17,0:00:07.65,Caption,,0,0,0,,momentum, tidal forcing and
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.65,0:00:09.12,Caption,,0,0,0,,the Earth–Moon barycenter.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.12,0:00:10.55,Caption,,0,0,0,,The best supported consequence
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.55,0:00:11.98,Caption,,0,0,0,,is this: ocean tides,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.98,0:00:13.40,Caption,,0,0,0,,axial stability and nights
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.40,0:00:14.83,Caption,,0,0,0,,would change on different
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.83,0:00:16.26,Caption,,0,0,0,,timescales.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.26,0:00:17.43,Caption,,0,0,0,,The exact timeline depends
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.43,0:00:18.61,Caption,,0,0,0,,on how the impossible
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.61,0:00:19.78,Caption,,0,0,0,,change occurs.
